# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ANGEL SWARM — .gitignore
#
# The working tree is ~2.7 GB. Almost none of that is source. This file keeps
# the repository to the application, the launcher source, the reproduction
# harnesses and the documents, and excludes four categories: things that are
# rebuilt from what is here, things that are large and derived, things that
# belong to somebody else, and scratch.
#
# Non-obvious entries carry a reason inline. Read those before deleting a line.
#
# REVISED 8 September 2026 for publication as DHA-OWHA-KM/DHA-ANGEL-SWARM-DEV.
# Two changes from the v6.5 package copy, both marked REVISED below and both
# made so that a plain ZIP download of this repository is a working program:
# the eight prebuilt launcher binaries are now TRACKED, and train/train.log is
# re-admitted. Several ignore blocks below name directories (OUT/, TEAMMATE/,
# BACKUP/, DECK/, shots*/) that are not present in this repository at all; they
# are kept so that re-importing the full working tree cannot re-admit them by
# accident. Nothing else was altered.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Dependencies ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1.4 GB. app/vendor/ holds the handful of files the application actually
# loads at runtime and those ARE tracked; node_modules is only the source they
# were vendored from. package.json + package-lock.json restore it.
node_modules/

# ── Compiled launcher binaries — TRACKED, deliberately ───────────────────────
# REVISED 8 September 2026 for repository publication. The v6.5 package ignored
# these on the reasoning that the source is the artefact and `go build` on
# go 1.24 reproduces them within 1% with no module downloads. That reasoning is
# still correct, and it is still the wrong trade HERE: this repository's first
# requirement is that "Download ZIP -> unzip -> run" works for a reviewer who
# has no Go toolchain. Eight binaries, ~33 MB, none near GitHub's 50 MB warning
# threshold. They are tracked on purpose. Build them yourself if you would
# rather not trust them — see the Quick start in README.md.
#
# GitHub's ZIP export does not preserve the Unix execute bit. macOS and Linux
# users need one `chmod +x` after unzipping. Windows is unaffected.
/ANGEL-SWARM

# ── Someone else's repository ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TEAMMATE/ contains a full clone of another person's project, provided for
# review. Publishing it here would be republishing their code under this
# repository's name and licence. It is excluded on purpose. Do not remove this
# line without that person's written permission. (See RESEARCH/GITHUB-PREP.md,
# decision 3.)
TEAMMATE/

# ── Release archives and backups ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# 599 MB of packaged release zips and 240 MB of dated tarball snapshots of a
# tree that git is about to version properly. Several BACKUP tarballs are
# ~61 MB, which trips GitHub's 50 MB per-file warning. Publish releases as
# GitHub Releases, not as tracked files.
BACKUP/
OUT/*.zip
*.tar.gz
*.zip

# ── Generated document formats ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every OUT/*.docx is generated from the OUT/*.md beside it. Track the source.
OUT/*.docx

# ── Large derived media ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 113 MB of renders. The four films the application itself plays live in
# app/video/ and ARE tracked, because the film pane loads them by relative
# path and the app breaks without them. These are the master and superseded
# cuts that nothing loads.
OUT/*.mp4
OUT/video/

# ── Screenshots, visual-regression output, design exploration ────────────────
# ~258 MB of PNG across the tree, all of it produced by the Playwright probe
# scripts to check a layout on a given day. None of it is an input to anything.
/*.png
shots/
shots3/
shots_dp/
shots_sha/
OUT/adapter-shots/
OUT/design-proof/
OUT/mapfix/
OUT/prov/
OUT/sec/
prov/
pal/
ref/
final-draft/
MOCKUPS/
mock/
MOCK/
mock-*.html
mock-*.png
spike/
spike-maplibre.html
# app/spike and app/spike-maplibre.html are symlinks into spike/ above; tracking
# them would commit links that dangle for every person who clones.
app/spike
app/spike-maplibre.html

# ── Presentation deck build ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DECK/ also contains jefferson.pptx — an unrelated internal work presentation
# ("API/KM Introduction and Recommendation") and its extracted contents under
# DECK/jx/, plus a DoD seal image. None of that is ANGEL SWARM and none of it
# should be published from this repository. (GITHUB-PREP.md, decision 6.)
# REVISED 8 September 2026: anchored to the repository root. Git on Windows
# sets core.ignorecase=true, which made the unanchored `DECK/` also match
# app/vendor/deck/ (deck.min.js, loaded at runtime by app/js/geo3d.js — the
# 3D map fails without it) and Documentation/deck/ (the ANGEL SWARM pitch
# decks). Neither was ever the target. The top-level DECK/ build directory
# still is, and is still not present in this repository.
/DECK/
.deckbuild/
.dtwork/

# ── One-off probe, measurement and packaging scripts ─────────────────────────
# ~250 single-purpose Playwright/node scripts written to answer one question on
# one day. The harnesses the documents actually cite are re-admitted below:
# winprob.mjs (the win table), _sbom_gen.mjs / _sbom_validate.mjs (the SBOM) and
# _sec_verify.mjs (the security measurements). app/selftest.html is inside app/
# and was never ignored.
/_*.mjs
/_*.js
!/_sbom_gen.mjs
!/_sbom_validate.mjs
!/_sec_verify.mjs
!/_sec_regress.mjs
/v3_*.mjs
/v5*.mjs
/v6*.mjs
/v7*.mjs
/v8_*.mjs
/dp_*.mjs
/sha_*.mjs
/thx_*.mjs
/fleetsweep_*.mjs
/fleetsweep_*.json
/wg_*.mjs
/wg_*.txt
/shot*.mjs
/verify*.mjs
/measure*.mjs
/audit*.mjs
/probe*.mjs
/base[0-9].mjs
/z[0-9].mjs
/za.mjs
/t[12]*.mjs
/dp_out/
/dp_out2/
/dp_cold/
/_cw/
/_chrome/
/_mapagent/
/_mapagent*/

# ── Scratch and OS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REVISED: `*.log` is narrowed so it does not swallow train/train.log, which is
# the record of the CRI-Net training run and ships as evidence.
*.log
!train/train.log
*.pre-*
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.venv/
venv/

# ── Fetched at runtime, never committed ──────────────────────────────────────
# get-model.sh / get-model.ps1 download the optional Qwen2.5-0.5B GGUF here.
# ~400 MB, Apache-2.0, and deliberately not redistributed in this repository.
app/models/llm.gguf
app/models/*.part
